  "reason": "The strongest result so far is config_010 (scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, multiprofile, avgpool, concat) at 0.715 accuracy, which dwarfs all other configs. The key question is whether a more expressive aggregation strategy can push performance further. With scgpt, avgpool (0.518) marginally beat transformer (0.507), but that gap was small (~1%) and based on a much weaker RNA encoder. With scvi_n200 producing far richer profile representations, transformer aggregation could capture non-linear inter-profile interactions that simple averaging misses. Config_007 is a single-variable change from the best config (avgpool → transformer), keeping all other winning components (scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, multiprofile, concat). This is the most focused exploitation of the strongest evidence while testing the highest-impact remaining design choice. With 3 experiments left after this, a clear signal here would guide the final experiments toward either further refinement or confirming the optimum."
}

